<p>An Austrian court in Innsbruck convicted a 37-year-old amateur climber of manslaughter after his girlfriend died of hypothermia during a January 2025 climbing trip on Grossglockner, Austria’s highest mountain. The court handed down a suspended prison sentence and a fine, according to reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/V-jdB_ap5nf-f75st-0xl-DAdtJ0ipnJFDdEvH96Q5HAVMzr6lx_FQPKC2jaUQmrV1RliVTk6tVmWUq7YMVHKpqZXmMMoA2_eMq8MGhq2m0Jb2nYv2ITJf7XimAEydP_HCTVGiemtRkQrnNCSG1u_UfNTXXXp9sSTzXg6KFyFMuGJ-LFavJ9p7Gec5Mf05NqE4OFTJQKha9FEvQtNFZaEHRT-I3uS1z8W9ir6zgvxlblg6Coc9LWPLmVWi-ha77fII-E6kNBVJj7kmnWtAwn' alt='Grossglockner, Austria’s highest peak, where the fatal climb occurred.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Penalty specifics: The Guardian and SCMP both reported a five-month suspended sentence and a €9,400 fine.</li><li>Incident detail: Reports said the woman ran into trouble near the summit area, and prosecutors argued that a series of poor decisions helped lead to the fatal outcome.</li><li>Identification in coverage: The New York Times identified the defendant as Thomas Plamberger, while other outlets referred to him as Thomas P; some outlets named the woman as Kerstin G.</li><li>How unusual the case is: SCMP noted that prosecutions over climbing accidents are rare, even when authorities allege a string of mistakes.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Court (Innsbruck): The court convicted the climber of manslaughter and gave him a suspended prison sentence and a fine, according to reports. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/20/austria-climber-convicted-manslaughter-girlfriend-kerstin-g-grossglockner-mountain'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3344054/climber-convicted-manslaughter-after-girlfriend-freezes-death-austrian-mountain'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Deutsche Welle: DW highlighted that he left his girlfriend on the peak while he went to find help, treating that decision as central to the conviction. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/austrian-climber-guilty-of-manslaughter-after-leaving-girlfriend-on-alpine-peak/a-76051539'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The New York Times framed the ruling as a boundary-setting case for when a partner’s choices during mountaineering can create criminal liability. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/europe/austrian-man-girlfriend-death-mountain-hike-guilty.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0k1xkllknmo'>Austrian climber found guilty after girlfriend froze to death on mountain</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/austrian-climber-guilty-of-manslaughter-after-leaving-girlfriend-on-alpine-peak/a-76051539'>Austrian climber guilty of manslaughter after leaving girlfriend on Alpine peak</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/europe/austrian-man-girlfriend-death-mountain-hike-guilty.html'>Austrian Man Found Guilty in Girlfriend’s Death on Mountain Hike</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3344054/climber-convicted-manslaughter-after-girlfriend-freezes-death-austrian-mountain'>Climber convicted after girlfriend freezes to death on Austrian mountain</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/climber-is-convicted-over-girlfriends-death-near-austrias-highest-peak'>Climber is convicted over girlfriend’s death near Austria’s highest peak</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/20/austria-climber-convicted-manslaughter-girlfriend-kerstin-g-grossglockner-mountain'>Climber convicted of manslaughter after leaving girlfriend on Austria’s highest peak to get help</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>